# Byteman observation rule, cluster tier of group-by-row-limit-incrementRowCount-rowsCounted--autonomous (case-file amendment A7). Observation only: it changes nothing.
# Loaded at node start with  -javaagent:<byteman.jar>=script:<this file>  -Dstage4.trace=<file>
# One line per local sub-page read of a GROUP BY query, written when the counter is closed (end of that read):
#   GB ms=<epoch ms> rows=<rowsCounted> groups=<groupCounted> unfinished=<hasUnfinishedGroup> done=<isDone()>
# rows = rows that passed the counter in this read (<= rowLimit = page size P); groups = groups completed in this read; done = groupCounted >= groupLimit
# (for the target DataLimits.java:986, rowsCounted >= rowLimit). PagingGroupByAwareCounter inherits onClose, so continuation reads are traced as well.

RULE b78 row limit observation
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.db.filter.DataLimits$CQLGroupByLimits$GroupByAwareCounter
METHOD onClose
AT EXIT
IF TRUE
DO traceOpen("b78", java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.trace", "b78.trace"));
   traceln("b78", "GB ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis() + " rows=" + $0.rowsCounted + " groups=" + $0.groupCounted + " unfinished=" + $0.hasUnfinishedGroup + " done=" + $0.isDone())
ENDRULE
